Why Is Demand Increasing?

The market is benefiting from the growing adoption of intelligent sensing across autonomous driving, industrial automation, healthcare and connected electronics.

Camera-based sensing remains a leading segment because vision systems are increasingly used for perception, monitoring and automated decision-making.

Autonomous driving is another major application area. Local processing allows vehicles and other systems to interpret sensor information rapidly while reducing communication requirements.

Industrial automation and smart manufacturing are also expanding the use of edge intelligence, particularly where real-time decisions and continuous monitoring are required.

Fab & Technology Pulse

Technology development is moving toward sensor-level inference, TinyML and low-power multimodal edge intelligence. Greater integration between sensing hardware and AI processing is helping manufacturers develop smaller and more efficient intelligent devices.

The competitive focus is shifting toward low-power operation, processing efficiency, integration and reliable performance.

